Kanzo behind a reverse proxy (Umbrel, Docker, Cloudflare Tunnel, ...).

Umbrel terminates HTTP itself and forwards the browser's own Host header
(`umbrel.local:4290`) to the app, untouched. Kanzo's DNS-rebinding guard only
accepts localhost, IP literals and the machine's own names, on its own port, so
every request through the proxy is answered with 403.

This adds KANZO_TRUST_PROXY=1: the guard accepts the proxy's Host, and an Origin
is accepted when its authority matches that Host, over http or https. Anything
else is still refused, so a cross-site page cannot drive the API.

Only set it when a proxy is a sole way into the board.
